"vault.title" = "Passcode vault";
"vault.body" = "Hisn makes a Screen Time passcode and keeps it from you until the date you choose. If you set it as your Screen Time passcode and set Deleting Apps to Don't Allow (steps 1 and 2), apps, Hisn included, cannot be deleted and Screen Time cannot be changed before then. Hisn cannot check that you did. No second person is needed.";
"vault.duration" = "Keep it sealed for";
"vault.acknowledge" = "I understand I will not see this passcode again until the date, and Hisn cannot show it early.";
"vault.create" = "Create a passcode";
"vault.confirmTitle" = "Seal a Screen Time passcode?";
"vault.confirmBody %lld" = "Hisn will show a new passcode for 15 minutes so you can set it in Screen Time. After that it stays hidden for %lld days.";
"vault.steps" = "1. Settings › Screen Time › Lock Screen Time Settings: enter this passcode twice.\n2. Screen Time › Content & Privacy Restrictions: turn on, then App Store purchases › Deleting Apps › Don't Allow.\n3. Optional: Content & Privacy Restrictions › Web content › Limit Adult Websites.\n4. Come back and tap Seal.";
"vault.hidesSoon" = "It hides itself 15 minutes after it was made, even if you do not tap Seal.";
"vault.seal" = "I've set it — seal it now";
"vault.sealed" = "Passcode sealed";
"vault.sealedUntil" = "Hidden until";
"vault.extend" = "Keep it a week longer";
"vault.extendTitle" = "Keep the passcode a week longer?";
"vault.extendBody" = "This adds 7 days to the date. It cannot be shortened afterwards.";
"vault.due" = "The date has passed";
"vault.unseal" = "Show the passcode";
"vault.revealedBody" = "This is your Screen Time passcode. You can now change Screen Time or delete apps.";
"vault.forget" = "Forget this passcode";
"vault.limitsTitle" = "What this can and cannot stop";
"vault.limits" = "Apple lets the adult who set a Screen Time passcode reset it with their Apple Account password, and erasing the iPhone removes everything. If someone else organizes your Family Sharing, the reset needs their account instead. Showing the passcode needs the date to have passed on this iPhone and on Apple's server time, so moving the clock does not open it. The passcode is kept only on this device, outside backups.";
